issue : we have create AVD pool with 4x VM and each VM allow 12 session. I noticed that if the user simply leaves the Remote Desktop session open, it stays connected indefinitely. I'm wondering if there is Idle time settings to force log off a user after user Idle for one hour
 
provided below solution to the cx:
 
I have thoroughly reviewed your case statement, and I am pleased to inform you that you can indeed configure Idle Timeout settings in Azure Virtual Desktop (AVD) to automatically log off users after a certain period of inactivity. This approach is beneficial for freeing up session capacity and improving resource utilization.
 
Here’s a step-by-step guide to create a Group Policy Object (GPO) that enforces an idle timeout for Remote Desktop sessions in your AVD session host VMs. The goal here is to log off users after 1 hour of inactivity. 
 
Steps to Create the GPO:
 
1. Open Group Policy Management: On your domain controller or management server, open the Group Policy Management Console (GPMC) from Start > Administrative Tools > Group Policy Management.
   
2. Create a New GPO: Right-click your Organizational Unit (OU) that contains the AVD session hosts. Select “Create a GPO in this domain, and Link it here…”. Name it something like: AVD - Idle Timeout Policy.
 
3. Edit the GPO: Right-click the new GPO and choose Edit.
 
4. Navigate to Session Time Limits: Go to: Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > Windows Components > Remote Desktop Services > Remote Desktop Session Host > Session Time Limits.
 
5. Configure Idle Timeout: Double-click "Set time limit for active but idle Remote Desktop Services sessions". Set it to Enabled and set the time limit to 1 hour.
 
6. End Session When Time Limit is Reached: Double-click "End session when time limits are reached". Set it to Enabled.
 
7. (Optional) Configure Other Limits: You can also configure additional settings such as "Set time limit for disconnected sessions" and "Set time limit for active sessions".
 
**Steps to Configure Idle Timeout via Intune:**
 
1. Sign in to Microsoft Intune Admin Center: Go to: [Microsoft Intune Admin Center](https://intune.microsoft.com).
 
2. Create a New Configuration Profile: Navigate to Devices> Configuration profiles and click + Create profile. Choose: Platform: Windows 10 and later, Profile type: Templates > Custom.
 
3. Name the Profile: Give it a name like: AVD Idle Timeout Policy.
 
4. Add OMA-URI Settings: Click Add to create a new custom setting.
 
   - First Setting: Idle Timeout
     - Name: Idle Timeout
     - OMA-URI: ./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/RemoteDesktopServices/MaxIdleTime
     - Data type: Integer
     - Value: 3600000 (this is 1 hour in milliseconds)
 
   - Second Setting: End Session When Time Limit is Reached
     - Name: End Session
     - OMA-URI: ./Device/Vendor/MSFT/Policy/Config/RemoteDesktopServices/EndSessionWhenTimeLimitsReached
     - Data type: Boolean
     - Value: true
 
5. Save and Assign the Profile: Click Next, assign the profile to the device group that contains your AVD session hosts, and click Create.
 
Once applied, this policy will ensure that users are automatically logged off after 1 hour of inactivity on Entra-joined AVD session hosts.
 
